Cached the profile pointer and added `__builtin_expect` hints so the rare null/out-of-range returns are placed out of line, keeping the hot decode path straight-line.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 Field::GetScale() const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return 1.0;
    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex >= p->numFields, 0))
        return 1.0;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].scale;
}
```